%!PS
% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 EfterScript contributors
% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% Scenario: data that ends early. A 4x4 grey image interleaved by
% separate sources: the mask is complete, but the data procedure returns
% one row, then another, then an empty string. The image is cut to its
% upper half, masked by the upper half of the mask (its two middle
% columns kept off), with no error; the lower half shows the backdrop.
/backdrop {
  0.3 setgray 0 0 1 1 rectfill
  0 setgray 0 0.25 0.75 { 0 0.125 1 rectfill } for
} def
/rows [<F0F0F0F0> <C0C0C0C0> <>] def
/next 0 def
gsave
100 400 translate 200 200 scale
backdrop
<< /ImageType 3 /InterleaveType 3
   /DataDict << /ImageType 1 /Width 4 /Height 4 /BitsPerComponent 8
      /ImageMatrix [4 0 0 -4 0 4] /Decode [0 1]
      /DataSource { rows next get /next next 1 add def } >>
   /MaskDict << /ImageType 1 /Width 4 /Height 4 /BitsPerComponent 1
      /ImageMatrix [4 0 0 -4 0 4] /Decode [0 1]
      /DataSource <60606060> >> >> image
grestore
showpage
